    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` field existed only in the acceptance spec \u2014 it wasn't in the schema, model, or mapper. I wired it in at the two natural layers:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema: a read-only string enum (`SILVER` / `BRONZE`). The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` and a `membershipTier(Owner)` default method implementing the rule:\n\n```java\ndefault OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n    Integer namesakeCount = owner.getNamesakeCount();\n    boolean unique = namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0;\n    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n    return unique && hasEmail ? OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.SILVER\n            : OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.BRONZE;\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the same derived-field pattern already used for `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber`, so the GET-owner pipeline (`RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`) picks it up with no YAML changes. `SILVER` requires `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email present; everything else (namesakes exist, or no email) is `BRONZE`.",
